{
  "requirement": "Each assessment MUST have a separate JSON usage record under\n`<state-root>/authoring/usage/<run-id>.json` using\n{cite}`requirements.configuration.state_location`.\nIt MUST identify its format version, run, project root, subject kind and full\nname, start time, backend and model when known, end time when finished, outcome,\naccepted determination kind (`true`, `false`, or `FIXME`) when present, and\nwhether evidence was written. It MUST record the selected output destination in\n`evidence_output` as `file` or `stdout`; a successful write to either destination\nMUST set `evidence_written` to true. Usage recording MUST remain outside the\nproject in stdout mode. FIXME entry text MUST NOT be stored in usage records.\nFailed, cancelled, or unfinished\nruns MUST remain distinguishable from completed judgments. Records MUST persist\nfor later review without storing source text, prompts, responses, or rationale.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judged the tests adequate for `requirements.authoring.usage_storage`. I did not request any implementation source. The marked tests give each obligation a scenario and an assertion, as follows.\n\n- **Separate record per assessment at `<state-root>/authoring/usage/<run-id>.json`.**\n  - `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[usage_record_identifies_its_run_and_unusable_state_is_reported]` reads the directory `<state>/habeas/authoring/usage` and finds one file. It asserts the file is named `{run_id}.json`. A second `--force` run leaves the first file byte-identical and adds a second file.\n  - `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[citation_reviews_are_confirmed_with_fresh_targeted_conversations]` and `tests/authoring_batch.rs#fn[confirm_runs_a_second_assessment_with_its_own_usage_record]` check distinct run ids and separate records.\n  - The batch tests check one record per assessment (6 records for 6 subjects).\n- **Identifying fields.**\n  - `usage_record_identifies_its_run_and_unusable_state_is_reported` asserts `version`, `run_id`, `project_root` (the canonicalized path), `subject`, `subject_kind`, `backend`, `model`, `evidence_output`, and `start_time_ms <= end_time_ms`.\n  - `usage_subject_kind_is_known_before_sources_are_prepared` covers the four subject kinds: requirement, example, citation review, and site review.\n  - `usage_record_of_an_early_failure_identifies_its_subject_kind` checks the subject kind on a failure before sources are prepared.\n- **Outcome and determination kind.**\n  - `stdout_emits_only_evidence_json_without_changing_project_files` loops over `true`, `false`, and `FIXME` and asserts `usage[\"determination\"]` equals each kind.\n  - `false_is_a_completed_assessment` and `ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free` repeat this for the file destination.\n  - The determination is null when absent: `missing_duplicate_and_invalid_submissions_preserve_existing_evidence` asserts it for failed runs, and the unit test `failed_persistence_records_failure_or_cancellation_and_retains_the_cause` asserts it for failed persistence.\n- **`evidence_output` and `evidence_written`.**\n  - The stdout test asserts `evidence_output == \"stdout\"` and `evidence_written == true`.\n  - The ollama CLI test and the batch tests assert `evidence_written == true` for the file destination.\n  - `missing_duplicate_and_invalid_submissions_preserve_existing_evidence` asserts `evidence_output` is `file` or `stdout` and `evidence_written == false` for failed runs in both modes.\n  - `failed_evidence_write_keeps_the_accepted_judgment_in_usage` asserts `evidence_written == false`, outcome `failed`, and the kept FIXME determination.\n- **Usage stays outside the project, including in stdout mode.** `usage_state_inside_the_project_is_refused_before_creating_it` runs both the default and `--stdout` modes with the state root set inside the project. Both fail with the \"must be outside the project repository\" message, create nothing, and leave the evidence unchanged.\n- **FIXME text is not stored.**\n  - `ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free` submits `FIXME:[\"example/app#125\"]` and asserts the serialized usage record does not contain `#125`.\n  - The same test asserts the record does not contain the `github_issues` field.\n- **Failed, cancelled, and unfinished are distinguishable.**\n  - `usage.rs#cancelled_request_persists_elapsed_time_and_incomplete_totals` asserts the initial record is `unfinished` with a null end time. After `finish(\"cancelled\")` it asserts the outcome `cancelled` and a non-null end time.\n  - `failed_persistence_records_failure_or_cancellation_and_retains_the_cause` maps `PermissionDenied` to `failed` and `Interrupted` to `cancelled`. It also covers the case where the usage file itself cannot be written.\n  - The batch tests assert 1 `failed` and 5 `completed` records, and `a_denied_mandatory_input_aborts_only_its_assessment` asserts a `failed` record with no requests.\n- **Content-free records.**\n  - `input_metadata_counts_components_and_reads_without_persisting_source` asserts that source text, requirement text, file names, items, match names, term text, and builtin text are all absent from the serialized record.\n  - `tool_outcomes_are_distinct_and_unknown_names_do_not_leak_model_text` asserts that model-supplied tool names are absent.\n  - The ollama CLI test asserts that the requirement, definition, source payload, rationale, and credential are absent.\n  - The workspace configuration test asserts that the literal API key is absent.\n- **Cited `requirements.configuration.state_location`.** `usage_record_identifies_its_run_and_unusable_state_is_reported` shows records land under `<XDG_STATE_HOME>/habeas/...`. It shows that an unusable state location (a file blocking `XDG_STATE_HOME`, or no `XDG_STATE_HOME` and no `HOME`) is reported, before any model request, with nonzero exit and unchanged evidence. I did not reassess the cited requirement's own tests, such as Windows `LOCALAPPDATA`.\n\nI found no unexercised obligation and no acknowledged gap, and none is needed.",
  "references": "6ab89cf2424f541973fefc396f9941d70200aa208d2c88f2a9f023dbf0b5646b",
